  "preamble": "Deretroflexion of the retroflex ejective affricate [ʈʂʼ] to the alveolar ejective [t͡sʼ] in Georgian, merging it with the dental ejective. Wiktionary reconstructs a Proto-Kartvelian ejective *c̣₁ (subscript-1 series) whose reflex is c̣ (წ) in Old and Modern Georgian but č̣ (ჭ) in Laz, Mingrelian and Svan: *mc̣₁er- 'fly' gives Old Georgian მწერი mc̣eri 'insect, fly' beside Mingrelian ჭანდი č̣andi, and *anc̣₁l- 'dwarf elder' gives Georgian ანწლი anc̣li beside Laz and Mingrelian ინჭირი inč̣iri and Svan გა̈ნჭუ̂ gänč̣û. Wikipedia's Proto-Kartvelian consonant table, citing Gamkrelidze (1966: 70) and Fähnrich (2002: 5), gives *c̣₁ the value [t͡ʂʼ], distinct from *c̣ [t͡sʼ] and *č̣ [t͡ʃʼ]. The retroflex value belongs to that reconstruction; the cognates themselves show only that Georgian c̣ corresponds to Zan and Svan č̣ in these words.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Deretroflexion, Merger, Fronting",
